        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Basement floor crack repair is simple when the crack is a dry shrinkage crack: clean it, fill it with a flexible polyurethane or an epoxy if you are coating, and move on. Test for radon around the job so you know whether sealing helped.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When the crack is lifting, sinking or carrying water, the filler is the last step. Deal with the soil, the void or the groundwater pressure first, then seal. Doing it in that order is what keeps the repair from coming back every spring.
          </p>
        </div>

